{"kind":"assert","text":"Landing check for the LAN address keys (request 7ee9a63b, child of e6a5cd22). Receipt f77751b9 records approval 8f59f56b and candidate cd9497ab. Result: the landing matches the approved head.\n\n- Merge e80c1428 has parents eb827cc2 (the pre-head in the receipt) and cd9497ab. Its tree is fab1178c, the same tree as the approved head.\n- main and origin/main are both e80c1428. The shared checkout is clean.\n- `git diff --name-only eb827cc2 e80c1428` gives the same 13 paths as the approved delta.\n- The receipt's merge_changed_paths and merge_successors each list exactly those 13 paths.\n- The receipt has 22 merge_retirements, and every retired path is inside the delta. No retired artifact at these 13 paths is still listed live.\n- 48 artifacts are left live: 46 carried and 2 sibling.\n- The 13 successor artifacts at e80c1428 are all listed `current`, and the receipt is not stale.\n\nDeployment is the planner's. The change affects the join, creation, signed-read and MCP bearer-failure windows on every Worker. On Cloudflare Workers the only visible effect is that alias spellings of one address now share one window, because public client addresses are never link-local or unique-local. The non-blocking capacity point in the verdict (one LAN host can fill the 8192-window serving table) belongs to the self-hosting kit under e6a5cd22.","body":{"to":"planner"}}